course: dictionary
lesson: 6325
title: Motive: why people do things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A motive is the reason someone does something. In «The Badger looked at him very suspiciously, but Toad's frank, open countenance made it difficult to suggest any unworthy motive», the Badger cannot think of any bad reason for Toad's actions, because Toad's face looks honest and open. Countenance means face.
explain: Look for clue words. Motive often comes with for or behind, as in «a motive for» and «the motive behind». A detective might ask, «Who had a motive?», which means who had a reason to do it. Try swapping in the word reason: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
explain: A motive is often secret. A hidden motive or an ulterior motive is a reason someone keeps to themselves. When you read a story, ask yourself why a character acts as they do, and whether they might have a hidden motive.
explain: Motive can also be an adjective in science. Motive power is the power that causes movement. Steam gave motive power to trains, pushing them along the track.
fact: A motive is the reason why someone does something.
fact: «Motive» often means a secret or wrong reason, as in «a hidden motive».
fact: «The motive behind» something is the reason that lies behind it.
fact: In science, «motive power» means power that causes movement, such as steam driving a train.
fact: A good check is to swap in the word «reason»: if the sentence still makes sense, «motive» means the same thing.
exercise: «The Badger could not suggest any unworthy motive.» What does motive mean here? | A very old kind of engine | A type of fish | A bright light in the dark | *The reason for doing something
exercise: A detective asks, «Who had a motive?» What is the detective asking? | *Who had a reason to do it? | Who can run the fastest? | Who is the tallest? | Who has the best hat?
exercise: In «motive power», motive is an adjective. What does it mean? | Very old | Hidden from view | Causing sadness | *Causing movement
test: Which phrase means a reason that someone keeps secret? | Motive power | *Hidden motive | Frank smile | Open countenance
test: Steam gave what to trains? | A quiet whisper | *Motive power | A motive for sleeping | A long countenance
exam: In «Toad's frank, open countenance made it difficult to suggest any unworthy motive», what does unworthy motive mean? | *A bad or dishonest reason | A good reason to be kind | A reason to be happy | A long, tiring journey
